 "intro": "The indefinido tells a finished event. The imperfect tells a habit or the background of the scene.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "ayer",
   "significado": "yesterday",
   "pron": "a-YER",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a closed day, so it goes with the indefinido: «ayer compré». The initial y sounds as in «yo».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "antes",
   "significado": "back then, before",
   "pron": "AN-tes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the imperfect it points to a habit: «antes viajaba en tren». It is the opposite of «ahora».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "compré",
   "significado": "I bought",
   "pron": "kom-PRE",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The accent marks the last syllable: kom-PRÉ. Without it, «compre» is a different verb form.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "compraba",
   "significado": "I/he/she used to buy",
   "pron": "kom-PRA-ba",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "-ar verbs form the imperfect with -aba. It talks about a habit: «compraba pan cada día».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "llovió",
   "significado": "it rained",
   "pron": "yo-BYO",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Llover» is only used in the third person. The ll sounds like y and the ó is the stressed syllable.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "llovía",
   "significado": "it was raining, it used to rain",
   "pron": "yo-BI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It paints the rain as the background of the scene: «llovía cuando salí». The accent is on the í.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "el billete",
   "significado": "the ticket",
   "pron": "el bi-YE-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain «billete» is used for train or plane. In many countries of America «boleto» or «pasaje» is used.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "todo el día",
   "significado": "all day",
   "pron": "TO-do el DI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a fixed time expression: «todo el día». With «ayer» it describes a whole episode.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "en tren",
   "significado": "by train",
   "pron": "en TREN",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With vehicles you say «en»: en tren, en bus, en avión. But «a pie» and «a caballo» take «a».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viajaba",
   "significado": "I/he/she used to travel",
   "pron": "bya-HA-ba",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Viajar is written with v and j, like «viaje». The j sounds like a soft h.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "salí",
   "significado": "I left, I went out",
   "pron": "sa-LI",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A single event: «salí de casa a las ocho». The accent marks the last syllable: sa-LÍ.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viajabas",
   "significado": "you used to travel (viajar)",
   "pron": "bya-HA-bas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The -abas ending is the imperfect for tú.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viajaste",
   "significado": "you travelled (viajar)",
   "pron": "bya-HAS-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The -aste ending is the past for tú: «viajaste» is one finished trip.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "saliste",
   "significado": "you left (salir)",
   "pron": "sa-LIS-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Salir» is regular in the past: «salí», «saliste».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "comprábamos",
   "significado": "we used to buy (comprar)",
   "pron": "kom-PRA-ba-mos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The accent shows the stress on -prá-, in the middle.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
