   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "An event or a habit",
     "texto": [
      "The choice depends on how you tell the past.\n\n- **Indefinido**: a **finished event**, an episode with a beginning and an end.\n- **Imperfecto**: a **habit**, an action **in progress**, or the **background** of the scene.\n\nLook:\n\n- Ayer **compré** un billete. (one purchase, finished)\n- Antes **viajaba** en tren. (a habit)\n- **Llovía** cuando **salí** de casa. (the rain is the background; **salí** is the event)\n- Ayer **llovió** todo el día. (the rain is a complete episode inside a closed day)\n\nA finished event can happen once or several times: what matters is that you tell it **as closed**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Two pasts side by side",
     "texto": [
      "Compare the two forms with the same verb:\n\n- **comprar**: **compré** (closed event) / **compraba** (habit)\n- **llover**: **llovió** (complete episode) / **llovía** (background)\n- **viajar**: **viajé** (one trip) / **viajaba** (habitual trips)\n\nWords that help:\n\n- Usually with the **indefinido**: **ayer, anoche, el lunes pasado, de repente**.\n- Usually with the **imperfect**: **antes, siempre, cada día, de niño**.\n\nWhen one action **interrupts** another, the one in progress goes in the imperfect and the interrupting one in the indefinido: **Llovía cuando salí.**"
     ],
